OL,3,GNEWSAScientists discover new ancient
OL,4,Acrocodile relative
OL,5,
OL,6,FA previously undiscovered relative of
OL,7,Fthe crocodile that lived about 170
OL,8,Fmillion years ago has been identified
OL,9,Fby scientists.
OL,11,FA team from the University of
OL,12,FPortsmouth and Hassan II University of
OL,13,FCasablanca found fossils of the ancient
OL,14,Freptile in Morocco's Atlas Mountains.
OL,16,FThe animal - which has been named
OL,17,Fctenosuchus tenuidens - had a distinct
OL,18,Flong and narrow snout filled with
OL,19,Fneedle-like teeth, unlike any of its
OL,20,Fknown relatives.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
